1. Code Changes
---------------
- In `kernel/src/idt.rs`:
  - `syscall_entry`: Read hardware-saved CS from stack slot `[rsp + 120]` and pass it
    in register `r8` (5th argument in SysV ABI) to `syscall_dispatch`.
  - `common_exc`: Read hardware-saved CS from stack slot `[rsp + 40]` and pass it
    in register `r8` to `user_fault` -> `proc_handle_user_fault`.
- In `kernel/src/proc.rs`:
  - Extended `ProcessExitReason::Fault` with `cs: u64`.
  - Extended `struct Process` with `last_syscall_cs: u64` and `last_fault_cs: u64`.
  - In `syscall_dispatch`, record `cur.last_syscall_cs = frame_cs`.
  - In `handle_user_fault`, record `proc.last_fault_cs = cs` and `Fault { ..., cs }`.
  - Added public accessors `proc::get_process_syscall_cs(pid)` and `proc::get_process_fault_cs(pid)`.
- In `kernel/src/trustselftest.rs`:
  - Added committed assertion:
    `novad_cs = proc::get_process_syscall_cs(proc::PID_NOVAD).unwrap_or(0)`
    Assert `(novad_cs & 3) == 3 && novad_cs == crate::gdt::USER_CODE as u64`
    (confirming hardware-saved CS = 0x3B, CPL 3).
  - Added committed assertion on `bad_priv` fault trap frame:
    `vector == 13 && (cs & 3) == 3 && cs == crate::gdt::USER_CODE as u64`.

